    {
      "raw_time": false,
      "body": "want to compare return rate vs users per counter, how to do it?",
      "sender": "72495e6509da46ca9f01ee7f4d0258f4",
      "id": "54c440b8-cc2b-424f-bd81-a87dbef7b2df",
      "type": "msg",
      "time": 1784934898.709978
    },
    {
      "type": "msg",
      "body": "```python\nresult = df.groupby('Country').agg(\n    Avg_Returns_Rate=('Returns_Rate', 'mean'),\n    User_Count=('Returns_Rate', 'count')\n).sort_values('Avg_Returns_Rate', ascending=False)\n\nprint(result)\n```\n\nTo visualize with dual y-axis:\n\n```python\nfig, ax1 = plt.subplots(figsize=(12, 5))\n\nax1.bar(result.index, result['User_Count'], color='skyblue', label='Users')\nax1.set_ylabel('User Count', color='skyblue')\nax1.tick_params(axis='y', labelcolor='skyblue')\n\nax2 = ax1.twinx()\nax2.plot(result.index, result['Avg_Returns_Rate'], color='red', marker='o', label='Avg Returns Rate')\nax2.set_ylabel('Avg Returns Rate', color='red')\nax2.tick_params(axis='y', labelcolor='red')\n\nplt.title('Return Rate vs Users per Country')\nplt.xticks(rotation=45)\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()\n```",
      "id": "ec153261-8088-40f0-afef-313318d41026",
      "mentions": [],
      "raw_time": false,
      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::OpenCodeAcpPersona",
      "time": 1784934904.9404826
