      "body": "what is use_label_encoder in XGboost?"
    },
    {
      "id": "c2306f74-a95c-46a9-a407-c1c682e56b61",
      "time": 1784994332.347587,
      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::OpenCodeAcpPersona",
      "type": "msg",
      "raw_time": false,
      "mentions": [],
      "body": "**Deprecated** in newer XGBoost versions. It was used to convert labels to 0,1,2... internally.\n\n## What It Did\n```python\n# Old way (deprecated)\nXGBClassifier(use_label_encoder=False, eval_metric='logloss')\n```\n\n## What to Use Now\n```python\n# New way (no need for use_label_encoder)\nXGBClassifier(eval_metric='logloss')\n```\n\nIf you have multi-class labels, just ensure they're integers (0, 1, 2...) before training.\n\n```python\nfrom sklearn.preprocessing import LabelEncoder\nle = LabelEncoder()\ny_encoded = le.fit_transform(y)  # Converts to 0, 1, 2...\n```"
    },
    {
      "raw_time": false,
      "sender": "72495e6509da46ca9f01ee7f4d0258f4",
